        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Generate Contacts Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_CONTACTS_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1778270172580",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779100000010_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a sales assistant generating a comprehensive summary of all contacts linked to an account, using only the provided workflow data without inventing facts. Produce the final output strictly in JSON object format with no extra text, commentary, markdown, or explanations.\n\nIn the JSON object, include a comprehensive summary of all contacts linked to the account, following these rules:\n\nFrom ContactRollup data:\n\n    - Identify contacts involved in Open Opportunities or Open Leads as \"Key Contacts\".\n    - Identify contacts involved in Recently Won Deals or Won Opportunities as \"Influential Contacts\".\n    - Use ContactRollup engagement attributes for engagement classification and activity analysis.\n\nFrom Contact data:\n\n    - Determine the Top Location by identifying the most frequently occurring contact location.\n    - Derive \"Top Functions\" from JobTitle, Department, Role, or Affinity where available.\n    - Derive \"Dominant Seniority Level\" from JobTitle and Affinity values.\n    - Use only actual contact data provided.\n\nEngagement Summary:\n\n- Calculate the percentage of contacts who are Highly Engaged, Moderately Engaged, and Low Engaged.\n- Classify every contact by evaluating all available engagement indicators together.\n- Always evaluate all of the following ContactRollup attributes before assigning engagement level:\n    - Open Opportunities\n    - Won Opportunities\n    - Open Leads\n    - Completed Activities\n    - Open Activities\n    - Last Call Made\n    - Last Email Sent\n    - Last Response Date\n    - Last Touch\n- Use both engagement volume and recency when calculating engagement level.\n- Highly Engaged:\nContacts with multiple recent engagement signals.\n    - Contacts actively associated with open opportunities, open leads, or recently won opportunities.\n    - Contacts with recent calls, emails, responses, or touch activity.\n    - Contacts with meaningful completed or ongoing activities.\n- Moderately Engaged:\n    - Contacts with partial engagement signals.\n    - Contacts with some activities or touchpoints, but lower activity volume or weaker recency.\n    - Contacts with limited opportunity/lead involvement.\n- Low Engaged:\n    - Contacts with minimal or outdated engagement signals.\n    - Contacts with little or no recent activities, communication, opportunities, or leads.\n- Ensure every contact is classified into exactly one engagement category after considering all listed attributes together.\n- List names of \"Key Contacts\" who fall under Low Engagement.\n- Do not skip engagement classification if some attributes are missing; use all available signals.\n\nSummary Generation Rules:\n\n- Generate actual business insights, not instructions or templates.\n- Summarize all contacts collectively using both Contact data and ContactRollup data.\n- Every bullet point must contain meaningful insights with quantitative details wherever available.\n- Each bullet point should contain 2–3 concise sentences.\n- Include:\n    - Key Contacts from open opportunities or open leads.\n    - Influential Contacts from recently won deals or won opportunities.\n    - Top Location across contacts.\n    - Top Functions and Dominant Seniority Level.\n    - Engagement distribution percentages for Highly Engaged, Moderately Engaged, and Low Engaged contacts.\n    - Names of Low Engaged Key Contacts.\n- Use only information present in the provided data.\n- Do not invent missing values or relationships.\n- Do not include recommendations, next steps, or account-level commentary.\n- Do not mention IDs; always use contact names only.\n- Do not mention the word \"rollup\".\n- Do not provide recommendations or action items.\n- Do not output placeholder text, templates, or instructions inside the summary field.\n- Strictly do not use strikethrough formatting.\n- Output compact HTML only using <ul> and <li> tags with no newline characters.\n\n\n\nFormatting Rules:\n- Apply currency formatting using the symbol matching CurrencyCode (USD->$, EUR->€, GBP->£, JPY->¥).\n- Format amounts with K (thousand), M (million), B (billion) and one decimal place, dropping trailing\n  .0 (e.g., $15,000 → $15K; $3,200,000 → $3.2M; $1,450,000,000 → $1.45B).\n- Format dates as MMM DD, YYYY followed by a natural relative time from the current date (e.g.,\n  Oct 12, 2025, 1 day ago).\n- Do not include time, timezone, or hour/minute/second components.\n- If no valid date is available, omit it.\n\nStrictly follow this JSON output format:\n{\n\"summary\": \"<ul><li>Bullet point 1</li><li>Bullet point 2</li><li>Bullet point 3</li></ul>\"\n}\n\nUse the following data references:\n\n- Account search result: {{$context.$nodes.SEARCH_ACCOUNT.$output}}\n- Extracted account contacts: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_ACCOUNT_CONTACTS.$output.result}}\n- Contact search result: {{$context.$nodes.SEARCH_CONTACTS.$output}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1779100000010_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1779100000012",
            "name": "Get Top Contact Party IDs",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let result = {};\n\nfunction inferSeniorityRank(jobTitle) {\n  const title = String(jobTitle || \"\").toLowerCase().trim();\n  if (!title) return 0;\n\n  if (/\\b(chief|cxo|ceo|cfo|coo|cto|cio|cmo|cpo|president|founder|co-founder|partner)\\b/i.test(title)) return 8;\n  if (/\\b(evp|svp|executive vice president|senior vice president)\\b/i.test(title)) return 7;\n  if (/\\b(vp|vice president)\\b/i.test(title)) return 6;\n  if (/\\b(director)\\b/i.test(title)) return 5;\n  if (/\\b(manager|head of|group manager)\\b/i.test(title)) return 4;\n  if (/\\b(lead|senior|sr\\.?)\\b/i.test(title)) return 3;\n  if (/\\b(associate|specialist|analyst)\\b/i.test(title)) return 2;\n  if (/\\b(intern|trainee|junior|jr\\.?)\\b/i.test(title)) return 1;\n\n  return 0;\n}\n\nfunction toNumber(value) {\n  const n = Number(value);\n  return Number.isFinite(n) ? n : 0;\n}\n\nfunction getRollup(contact) {\n  return contact?.ContactRollup || {};\n}\n\ntry {\n  const rawContacts = $context.$nodes?.SEARCH_CONTACTS?.$output;\n  const contacts = Array.isArray(rawContacts)\n    ? rawContacts\n    : Array.isArray(rawContacts?.items)\n      ? rawContacts.items\n      : [];\n\n  const rankedContacts = [];\n\n  for (const contact of contacts) {\n    const partyNumber = contact?.PartyNumber;\n    if (!partyNumber) continue;\n\n    const rollup = getRollup(contact);\n\n    const wonRevenue = toNumber(rollup?.WonOpportunitiesRevenue);\n    const openRevenue = toNumber(rollup?.SumOfOpenOpportunitiesRevenue);\n    const totalRevenue = wonRevenue + openRevenue;\n\n    const numberOfOpenOpportunities = toNumber(rollup?.NumberOfOpenOpportunities);\n    const numberOfOpenLeads = toNumber(rollup?.NumberOfOpenLeads);\n    const numberOfTouches = toNumber(rollup?.NumberOfTouches);\n    const wonOpportunities = toNumber(rollup?.WonOpportunities);\n\n    const isKeyContact = numberOfOpenOpportunities > 0 || numberOfOpenLeads > 0;\n    const isInfluentialContact = wonOpportunities > 0;\n    const seniorityRank = inferSeniorityRank(contact?.JobTitle);\n\n    rankedContacts.push({\n      totalRevenue,\n      numberOfOpenLeads,\n      numberOfTouches,\n      isKeyContact,\n      isInfluentialContact,\n      seniorityRank,\n      partyNumber: String(partyNumber),\n      partyId: String(contact?.ContactPartyId ?? contact?.PartyId ?? \"\")\n    });\n  }\n\n  rankedContacts.sort((a, b) => {\n    if (b.totalRevenue !== a.totalRevenue) return b.totalRevenue - a.totalRevenue;\n    if (b.numberOfOpenLeads !== a.numberOfOpenLeads) return b.numberOfOpenLeads - a.numberOfOpenLeads;\n    if (b.numberOfTouches !== a.numberOfTouches) return b.numberOfTouches - a.numberOfTouches;\n    if (a.isKeyContact !== b.isKeyContact) return Number(b.isKeyContact) - Number(a.isKeyContact);\n    if (a.isInfluentialContact !== b.isInfluentialContact) return Number(b.isInfluentialContact) - Number(a.isInfluentialContact);\n    if (b.seniorityRank !== a.seniorityRank) return b.seniorityRank - a.seniorityRank;\n    if (a.partyNumber !== b.partyNumber) return String(a.partyNumber).localeCompare(String(b.partyNumber));\n    if (a.partyId !== b.partyId) return String(a.partyId).localeCompare(String(b.partyId));\n    return 0;\n  });\n\n  const top5 = rankedContacts.slice(0, 5);\n\n  result = {\n    top5ContactPartyNumbers: top5.map(c => c.partyNumber),\n    top5ContactPartyIds: top5.map(c => c.partyId),\n    contactCount: rankedContacts.length\n  };\n} catch (error) {\n  result = {\n    top5ContactPartyNumbers: [],\n    top5ContactPartyIds: [],\n    contactCount: 0,\n    error: String(error?.message || error)\n  };\n}\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778287840986",
            "failure": "end"
          },
          "code": "GET_TOP_CONTACT_PARTY_IDS",
          "id": "1779100000007",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
