                  "code": "CONTACTENGAGEMENTLLM",
                  "id": "1778394008684",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1778394008685_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "Input Data:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOPCONTACTS.GETACTIVITIES.$output}}\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOPCONTACTS.GETCALLS.$output}}\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOPCONTACTS.GETEMAILS.$output}}\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOPCONTACTS.GETNOTES.$output}}\n\nGOAL:\nAnalyze engagement data for a SINGLE CONTACT and generate a structured, contact-specific summary that reflects ONLY that contact’s behavior, preferences, and interaction signals.\n\nCRITICAL CONTEXT:\n- This prompt is executed PER CONTACT (inside a loop).\n- ALL input data belongs to ONE specific contact.\n- NEVER reference or infer other contacts.\n- The output MUST be strictly isolated to this contact only.\n\nCONTACT IDENTIFICATION (MANDATORY):\n- Extract and use the contact name wherever available in the input.\n- The \"summary\" MUST explicitly include the contact name.\n- If name is not explicitly available, refer consistently as \"The contact\" (do NOT hallucinate names).\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n- Carefully read and interpret the input data.\n- Classify insights strictly into these 4 buckets:\n  1. Sentiment\n  2. Product Focus\n  3. Industry Focus\n  4. Signals\n\n- Generate an overall \"summary\" that:\n  - Clearly describes THIS contact’s engagement behavior\n  - Includes contact name explicitly\n  - Covers responsiveness, tone, engagement level, and key patterns\n  - Highlights changes over time if present\n\nBUCKET STRUCTURE RULES:\n\n1. SENTIMENT:\n- Provide ONLY a \"summary\"\n- Reflect:\n  - Tone (positive / neutral / negative)\n  - Responsiveness\n  - Urgency\n  - Communication style\n- Keep concise and contact-specific\n\n2. PRODUCT FOCUS / INDUSTRY FOCUS / SIGNALS:\nEach MUST include:\n\n- \"summary\":\n  - High-level synthesis of the most important insights for THIS contact\n  - Must remain strictly contact-specific\n\n- \"details\":\n  - MUST include ALL relevant factual observations from input\n  - MUST NOT drop any information\n  - MUST include:\n    - Product names, features, solutions\n    - Explicit requests, questions, concerns\n    - Interaction behaviors (calls, emails, notes)\n    - Engagement patterns (follow-ups, delays, frequency)\n  - MUST be precise and factual (no assumptions)\n\nDETAILS RULES (CRITICAL):\n- No data loss allowed\n- Deduplicate only exact or clearly redundant statements\n- Preserve specificity and context\n- Do NOT merge unrelated facts\n- Keep attribution implicitly tied to this contact\n\nCONTACT-SPECIFIC GUIDELINES:\n- Emphasize:\n  - Communication frequency and responsiveness\n  - Tone and sentiment shifts over time\n  - Preferences and interests\n  - Engagement level (active, passive, declining, increasing)\n  - Influence or role indicators (if present)\n- DO NOT generalize beyond this contact\n- DO NOT introduce account-level aggregation unless explicitly stated\n\nNO CROSS-CONTACT CONTAMINATION:\n- DO NOT reference multiple contacts\n- DO NOT compare contacts\n- DO NOT use plural terms like \"contacts\", \"they\", \"others\"\n- EVERYTHING must describe ONE contact only\n\nMISSING DATA HANDLING:\n- If a bucket has no data:\n  - \"summary\": \"\"\n  - \"details\": \"\" (if applicable)\n\nGENERAL RULES:\n- Do NOT mix insights across buckets\n- Do NOT hallucinate\n- Keep summaries concise, factual, and structured\n- Ensure ALL fields are always present\n- Maintain consistency in terminology\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n{\n  \"contact_engagement\": {\n    \"summary\": \"string\",\n    \"sentiment\": {\n      \"summary\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"product_focus\": {\n      \"summary\": \"string\",\n      \"details\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"industry_focus\": {\n      \"summary\": \"string\",\n      \"details\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"signals\": {\n      \"summary\": \"string\",\n      \"details\": \"string\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nSTRICT OUTPUT RULES (CRITICAL):\n\n- Output MUST be raw JSON object\n- DO NOT wrap in markdown\n- DO NOT return as string\n- DO NOT escape quotes\n- DO NOT add backticks\n- DO NOT add newline escape characters (\\n)\n- Response must start with { and end with }"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                }
              ],
              "rootNode": "start_1778393444925"
