        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "consolidateContactEng"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "CONSOLIDATECONTACTENG",
          "id": "1778403552679",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778403552680_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input Data:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOPCONTACTS.$output}} \n\nGOAL:\nConsolidate multiple contact_engagement summaries into a single unified structure WITHOUT losing any information, while ensuring the final output remains CONTACT-SPECIFIC and explicitly references CONTACT NAMES.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n- The input contains multiple objects, each with the same \"contact_engagement\" structure.\n- Each object corresponds to a specific contact (name may be present in input context or within summary/details).\n- Merge all entries into ONE final \"contact_engagement\" object.\n\nCRITICAL REQUIREMENT (CONTACT AWARENESS):\n- ALWAYS explicitly reference contact names in the final \"summary\" and wherever relevant.\n- DO NOT produce a generic or anonymous summary.\n- If multiple contacts exist, clearly distinguish them and describe their individual behaviors within the consolidated summary.\n- Preserve contact-level distinctions even while consolidating.\n\nMERGING RULES:\n\n1. OVERALL SUMMARY:\n- Generate a single consolidated \"summary\".\n- MUST explicitly mention contact names and their respective behaviors.\n- Compare and contrast contacts where applicable (e.g., \"John shows high engagement while Priya is less responsive\").\n- Reflect:\n  - Engagement patterns per contact\n  - Responsiveness per contact\n  - Tone shifts per contact\n  - Key behavioral differences across contacts\n- Highlight trends such as increasing/decreasing engagement PER CONTACT.\n\n2. SENTIMENT:\n- Combine all sentiment summaries.\n- Identify dominant sentiment overall AND note variations per contact.\n- MUST reference contact names when describing sentiment differences.\n- Provide a single concise but contact-aware summary.\n\n3. PRODUCT FOCUS, INDUSTRY FOCUS, SIGNALS:\nEach must contain:\n- \"summary\":\n  - High-level synthesis INCLUDING contact-specific mentions.\n  - Clearly indicate which contact is associated with which interest or signal.\n- \"details\":\n  - MUST include ALL unique factual points from every batch.\n  - Tag or associate facts with the correct contact wherever possible.\n\nDETAILS RULES (CRITICAL):\n- Do NOT drop any information.\n- Merge and deduplicate overlapping points.\n- Preserve:\n  - Product names\n  - Features\n  - Requests\n  - Behaviors\n  - Signals\n  - Contact-specific preferences\n- If multiple contacts share similar points, consolidate BUT still retain attribution if meaningful.\n\n4. NO DATA LOSS:\n- Every important fact from every batch must appear in the final output.\n\n5. NO DUPLICATION:\n- Avoid repeating identical statements.\n- Merge semantically similar content.\n\n6. CONTACT-SPECIFIC CONSOLIDATION GUIDELINES:\n- Emphasize per contact:\n  - Communication patterns (frequency, responsiveness)\n  - Tone and sentiment shifts\n  - Preferences and interests\n  - Engagement level (active, passive, declining, increasing)\n  - Influence or role signals\n- DO NOT generalize across contacts.\n- DO NOT blur distinctions between contacts.\n\n7. STRUCTURE:\n- Output ONLY ONE object.\n- Maintain EXACT same schema.\n\n8. STRICT OUTPUT:\n- Output must be valid JSON only.\n- No explanations, no extra text.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n{\n  \"summary\": \"string\",\n  \"sentiment\": {\n    \"summary\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"product_focus\": {\n    \"summary\": \"string\",\n    \"details\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"industry_focus\": {\n    \"summary\": \"string\",\n    \"details\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"signals\": {\n    \"summary\": \"string\",\n    \"details\": \"string\"\n  }\n}\n\nSTRICT OUTPUT RULES (CRITICAL):\n\n- Output MUST be raw JSON object.\n- DO NOT wrap output in ```json or any markdown.\n- DO NOT return as string.\n- DO NOT escape quotes.\n- DO NOT add backticks.\n- DO NOT add newline escape characters (\\n).\n- Strictly do not use strikethrough formatting.\n- Response must start with { and end with } only.\n- If a field has no supporting data, output exactly \"\". Do not generate filler, assumptions, risk statements, status labels, or placeholder phrases of any kind.\n- All keys defined in the output schema are mandatory and must be included even when no data is available; in such cases, use \"\" as the value.\n  Example fallback output when no data exists:\n  {\n  \"summary\": \"\",\n  \"sentiment\": {\n  \"summary\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"product_focus\": {\n  \"summary\": \"\",\n  \"details\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"industry_focus\": {\n  \"summary\": \"\",\n  \"details\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"signals\": {\n  \"summary\": \"\",\n  \"details\": \"\"\n  }\n  }"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
